---
import App from '../layouts/App.astro';
/* Rendered per request so the wallet selector gets a fresh CSP nonce (src/middleware.ts). */
export const prerender = false;
---
<App area="member" tab="holdings" title="Your shares" intro="Claim what your shares earned, sign split sheets for works you registered, and draft new shares. Look up any account without a wallet." description="Claim, approve split sheets and draft new shares with a NEAR testnet wallet.">
  <div class="member" data-member data-state="out">
    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="who-h">
      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="who-h">Account</h2><span class="end" data-who-badge><span class="badge plain">Not chosen</span></span></div>
      <div class="panel-body who-grid">
        <form class="field" data-lookup>
          <label for="acct-in">Look up an account, read only</label>
          <div class="inline"><input id="acct-in" name="account" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="writer-a.royltee-dev.testnet" /><button class="btn" type="submit">Look up</button></div>
          <p class="hint">Try writer-a.royltee-dev.testnet or buyer-pub.royltee-dev.testnet.</p>
        </form>
        <div class="field">
          <span class="label">Or act as yourself</span>
          <div class="actions"><button class="btn primary" type="button" data-connect>Connect a wallet</button><button class="btn quiet" type="button" data-disconnect hidden>Disconnect</button></div>
          <p class="hint">Your wallet signs each transaction. This site never sees a key.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="panel-foot" data-status aria-live="polite">Choose an account to begin.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" id="holdings" data-tab-panel aria-labelledby="claim-h">
      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="claim-h">Shares held</h2><span class="caption">Statement since mint, in mUSDC</span></div>
      <div data-held><div class="panel-body"><div class="empty"><p>Look up an account or connect a wallet to see the shares it holds and what each one can claim.</p></div></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" id="transfer" data-tab-panel aria-labelledby="tr-h">
      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="tr-h">Transfer a share</h2><span class="end"><span class="badge unv">UNVERIFIED</span></span></div>
      <div class="panel-body" data-transfer><div class="empty"><p>Choose an account first. The shares it holds can be sent to another verified member.</p></div></div>
      <p class="panel-foot">Only the holder can transfer, only to an active verified member, and never while a payout is in flight, a dispute is open or another transfer is pending. Approvals for marketplaces are disabled by design. Sending from this page has not been run on testnet yet; the recorded catalog sale of s2 was signed outside this site.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" id="org" data-tab-panel aria-labelledby="org-h">
      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="org-h">Organisation agents</h2><span class="end"><span class="badge warn">Needs the org wallet</span> <span class="badge unv">UNVERIFIED</span></span></div>
      <div class="panel-body" data-org><div class="empty"><p>Choose the organisation account first, for example buyer-pub.royltee-dev.testnet. Its wallet signs every control here; the agent never can.</p></div></div>
      <p class="panel-foot">The checks mirror the contract rules; the contract stays the authority and refuses anything outside them. Sending from this page has not been run on testnet yet; the recorded agent role was granted outside this site.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" id="approvals" data-tab-panel aria-labelledby="ap-h">
      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="ap-h">Split sheets to approve</h2><span class="caption">Shares other members registered on works this account registered</span><span class="end"><span class="badge info">Not sent from this site yet</span></span></div>
      <div data-approvals><div class="panel-body"><div class="empty"><p>Choose an account first. Shares that wait for its signature show up here.</p></div></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" id="draft" data-tab-panel aria-labelledby="draft-h">
      <div class="panel-head"><h2 id="draft-h">Draft a split sheet</h2><span class="end"><span class="badge unv">UNVERIFIED</span></span></div>
      <div class="panel-body" data-draft><p class="loading">Reading works</p></div>
      <p class="panel-foot">Sending from this page has not been run on testnet yet. Each row becomes one register_share call from your wallet with 0.2 NEAR attached. The contract takes 0.1 NEAR for the share account, 0.00125 NEAR for its token registration and the storage the record uses plus 1000 bytes reserved for the mint, and refunds the rest in the same call (whether 0.2 NEAR always covers it is UNVERIFIED on testnet). If the mint later fails because the holder lost its credential, or is released as stale, that NEAR is not refunded.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</App>
<script>import '../scripts/member.ts';</script>
<style is:global>
  .member { display: grid; gap: var(--s5); }
  .org-card { border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: var(--r-card); background: var(--surface); }
  .org-card-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: var(--s2) var(--s3); min-height: 2.75rem; padding: var(--s3) var(--s4); cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; }
  .org-card-head:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--focus, var(--ink)); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .org-card[open] > .org-card-head { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--edge); }
  .org-card-body { display: grid; gap: var(--s3); padding: var(--s4); }
  .org-card-head .end { margin-left: auto; }
  .org-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(12rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--s3); }
  .methods { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s2) var(--s5); }
  .methods legend { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-14); margin-bottom: var(--s2); }
  .methods label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--s2); min-height: 2.75rem; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: var(--fs-14); }
  .methods input { width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem; }
  .member [data-tab-panel] { scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
  .who-grid { grid-template-columns: 1.3fr 1fr; align-items: start; }
  .inline { display: flex; gap: var(--s2); }
  .inline input { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
  .checklist { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--s2); }
  .checklist li { display: flex; gap: var(--s3); align-items: baseline; font-size: var(--fs-14); }
  .checklist .badge { flex: none; min-width: 4.2rem; justify-content: center; }
  .review { border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: var(--r-card); padding: var(--s5); display: grid; gap: var(--s4); background: var(--surface-2); }
  .draft-rows td { padding-top: .4rem; padding-bottom: .4rem; }
  .draft-rows input, .draft-rows select { min-width: 8rem; }
  .draft-rows input[type="number"] { min-width: 6rem; text-align: right; font-family: var(--mono); }
  .draft-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s4); }
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .who-grid, .draft-meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .inline { flex-direction: column; }
    .claim-cell .btn { min-height: 2.75rem; }
    .draft-rows thead { display: none; }
    .draft-rows, .draft-rows tbody { display: block; }
    .draft-rows tr { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--s2); padding: var(--s3) var(--s4); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .draft-rows td { padding: 0 !important; border: 0 !important; height: auto; }
    .draft-rows td:first-child { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .draft-rows input, .draft-rows select { min-width: 0 !important; width: 100%; }
  }
</style>
